INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3462,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:41:53.516768','Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3463,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:41:55.557995','Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits. Portraying executive skills as "dysfunctional" presumes that there is a correct way to complete a task, however there may be multiple ways to complete a task that aren''t recognized or supported.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3464,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:41:57.774102','Disorder is considered a medical term often relating to definitions of chaos, disturbances, or irregularity. "Disorder" is also often used to refer to functioning labels that gatekeep accessibility support. "Disability" is preferred because of its more inclusive nature normalizing individual experiences with various conditions and focusing on the need for accessibility as the root of disability.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3465,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:41:59.933054','Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits. Commitment to ideas can be done and due to many reasons. Reasons it occurs are to mitigate anxiety or because of natural interest in becoming a subject expert.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3466,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:42:02.144430','Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits. Commitment to a subject can be done and due to many reasons. Reasons it occurs are to mitigate anxiety or because of natural interest in becoming a subject expert.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3467,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:42:05.084408','Refers to people with mental or psychiatric disabilities.','en','hyper-sensitive','a',0,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["hyper-sensitive"]','[{"word_type": "a", "lower_case": true, "lemmatize": true}]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'hyper-sensitive','default','default',1,1,'hyper-sensitive','a','["behavior_advanced"]',NULL,0);
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3468,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:42:06.207664','Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3469,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:42:09.954941','Loner is a label given or presumed by others. A Disabled person may not be willingly isolating themselves from others, and may be facing social isolation or lack of accessibility that can be misinterpreted as "being a loner." Additionally, various sensory related disabilities require a retreat in reaction to sensory overload. This is considered an accessibility support need and is not an act of optional isolation. Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits.\ToClarify:
