INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3472,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:42:17.747024','','en','manic','a',0,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["manic"]','[{"word_type": "a", "lower_case": true, "lemmatize": true}]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'manic','default','default',1,1,'manic','a','["behavior_advanced"]',NULL,0);
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3473,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:42:18.929683','While "neuroatypical" is not technically incorrect, it is not the preferred term used by the community. Identity-first is more common, however person-first is still used.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3474,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:42:20.258839','Disorder is considered a medical term often relating to definitions of chaos, disturbances, or irregularity. "Disorder" is also often used to refer to functioning labels that gatekeep accessibility support. "Disability" is preferred because of its more inclusive nature normalizing individual experiences with various conditions and focusing on the need for accessibility as the root of disability. There are various kinds of Neurobehavioral disabilities that can be identified and labeled in different ways depending on the qualities of the disability. It''s best to identify the disability as accurately as you possibly can.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3475,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:42:21.551407','Neurodiverse is often misdefined as being the umbrella term for people with disabilities and conditions that impact the way a person''s brain processes information to be atypical to that of the majority. However, "neurodiverse" is an umbrella term for all ways of brain processing, neurotypical and neurodivergent. "Neurodiverse" encompasses the diversity of all thought processing. If referring to neurodivergence the term is "neurodivergent."\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3476,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:42:23.124274','Neurodiversity is often misdefined as being the umbrella term for the disabilities and conditions that impact the way a person''s brain processes information to be atypical to that of the majority. However, "neurodiversity" is an umbrella term for all ways of brain processing, neurotypical and neurodivergent. "Neurodiversity" encompasses the diversity of all people. If referring to neurodivergent people, the umbrella term is "neurodivergence."\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3477,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:42:26.474622','','en','nutter','n',0,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["nutter"]','[{"word_type": "n", "lower_case": true, "lemmatize": true}]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'nutter','default','default',1,1,'nutter','n','["behavior_advanced"]',NULL,0);
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3478,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:42:27.905651','Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3479,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:42:31.672228','Various related disabilities have been relabeled to be identified as Autism or being on the Autism Spectrum. PDD-NOS is no longer a relevant term and is terms Autism or being on the Autism Spectrum. A majority of the Autistic community prefers identity-first language. A small minority prefers person-first language.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3480,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:42:35.504071','Various related disabilities have been relabeled to be identified as Autism or being on the Autism Spectrum. PDD-NOS is no longer a relevant term and is terms Autism or being on the Autism Spectrum. A majority of the Autistic community prefers identity-first language. A small minority prefers person-first language.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(3481,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 15:42:38.017472','Prefer to be alone is an assumption presumed by others. A Disabled person may not be willingly isolating themselves from others, and may be facing social isolation or lack of accessibility that can be misinterpreted as "preferring to be alone." Additionally, various sensory related disabilities require a retreat in reaction to sensory overload. This is considered an accessibility support need and is not an act of optional isolation. Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits.\ToClarify:
