INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4237,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:04:59.506311','Ability is largely based on and rooted in accessibility and support resources. There are many factors that impact learning and "ability" is a word that isn''t always the most appropriate. Focus is most appropriately reflected with words related to tangible skills.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4238,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:00.702531','Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits. Portraying a skill in a negative way assumes that the person cannot or won''t improve, however, many Disabled people can improve on skillsets with the appropriate accessibility support.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4239,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:01.920784','Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits. Portraying a skill in a negative way assumes that the person cannot or won''t improve, however, many Disabled people can improve on skillsets with the appropriate accessibility support.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4240,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:03.019275','Refers to people with physical or mobility disabilities. Considered ableist because many wheelchair-users experience wheelchairs, and other mobility aids, as liberating, since they enable freedom of movement, rather than confining or restrictive.','en','dyslexia','',0,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["dyslexia"]','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dyslexia','default','default',NULL,NULL,'dyslexia',NULL,'["learning_advanced"]',NULL,0);
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4241,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:04.337823','Refers to people who have survived burns and have visible scars from burns. Not considered offensive by all.','en','dyslexic','a',0,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["dyslexic"]','[{"word_type": "a", "lower_case": true, "lemmatize": true}]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dyslexic','default','default',1,1,'dyslexic','a','["learning_advanced"]',NULL,1);
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4242,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:06.747190','Disability is preferred because of its more inclusive nature normalizing individual experiences with various conditions and focusing on the need for accessibility as the root of disability. There are various kinds of Language-based Learning disabilities that can be identified and labeled in different ways depending on the qualities of the disability. It''s best to identify the disability as accurately as you possibly can. Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4243,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:09.642463','Disability is preferred because of its more inclusive nature normalizing individual experiences with various conditions and focusing on the need for accessibility as the root of disability. There are various kinds of Language processing disabilities that can be identified and labeled in different ways depending on the qualities of the disability. It''s best to identify the disability as accurately as you possibly can. Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4244,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:13.199311','Ability is largely based on and rooted in accessibility and support resources. There are many factors that impact learning and "ability" is a word that isn''t always the most appropriate. Focus is most appropriately reflected with words related to tangible skills.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4245,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:14.922727','Disability is preferred because of its more inclusive nature normalizing individual experiences with various conditions and focusing on the need for accessibility as the root of disability. There are various kinds of Learning disabilities that can be identified and labeled in different ways depending on the qualities of the disability. It''s best to identify the disability as accurately as you possibly can. "Differences" is not an appropriate term because everyone, regardless of disability, learns differently. Attributing "differences" to Disabled people singles out Disabled people as being atypical when there is not "typical." Additionally, in the U.K. "learning differences" is used to define what the rest of the world would define as "learning disabilities" and are not considered to be identified or treated. This is not largely supported by the disability community because it denies accessibility as the source of disability.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4246,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:16.665376','Disability is preferred because of its more inclusive nature normalizing individual experiences with various conditions and focusing on the need for accessibility as the root of disability. There are various kinds of Learning disabilities that can be identified and labeled in different ways depending on the qualities of the disability. It''s best to identify the disability as accurately as you possibly can. Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits. "Difficulties" is not an appropriate term because everyone, regardless of disability, learns differently. Attributing "difficulties" to Disabled people singles out Disabled people as being atypical when there is not "typical." Additionally, in the U.K. "learning difficulties" is used to define what the rest of the world would define as "learning disabilities" and are not considered to be identified or treated. This is not largely supported by the disability community because it denies accessibility as the source of disability.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4247,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:18.265899','Disorder is considered a medical term often relating to definitions of chaos, disturbances, or irregularity. "Disorder" is also often used to refer to functioning labels that gatekeep accessibility support. "Disability" is preferred because of its more inclusive nature normalizing individual experiences with various conditions and focusing on the need for accessibility as the root of disability. There are various kinds of Learning disabilities that can be identified and labeled in different ways depending on the qualities of the disability. It''s best to identify the disability as accurately as you possibly can.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4248,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:19.939066','Disability is preferred because of its more inclusive nature normalizing individual experiences with various conditions and focusing on the need for accessibility as the root of disability. There are various kinds of Learning disabilities that can be identified and labeled in different ways depending on the qualities of the disability. It''s best to identify the disability as accurately as you possibly can. Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4249,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:21.616943','Disability is preferred because of its more inclusive nature normalizing individual experiences with various conditions and focusing on the need for accessibility as the root of disability. There are various kinds of Learning disabilities that can be identified and labeled in different ways depending on the qualities of the disability. It''s best to identify the disability as accurately as you possibly can. Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits. Additionally, in the U.K. "learning issues" is used to define what the rest of the world would define as "learning disabilities" and are not considered to be identified or treated. This is not largely supported by the disability community because it denies accessibility as the source of disability.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4250,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:23.603351','Disability is preferred because of its more inclusive nature normalizing individual experiences with various conditions and focusing on the need for accessibility as the root of disability. There are various kinds of Learning disabilities that can be identified and labeled in different ways depending on the qualities of the disability. It''s best to identify the disability as accurately as you possibly can. Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4251,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:24.887447','Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits. Portraying a skill in a negative way assumes that the person cannot or won''t improve, however, many Disabled people can improve on skillsets with the appropriate accessibility support.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4252,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:27.413894','Disorder is considered a medical term often relating to definitions of chaos, disturbances, or irregularity. "Disorder" is also often used to refer to functioning labels that gatekeep accessibility support. "Disability" is preferred because of its more inclusive nature normalizing individual experiences with various conditions and focusing on the need for accessibility as the root of disability. There are various kinds of Reading disabilities that can be identified and labeled in different ways depending on the qualities of the disability. It''s best to identify the disability as accurately as you possibly can, especially since some reading disabilities may be caused by learning disabilities and others might be due to visual or intellectual disabilities.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4253,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:30.833202','Portraying qualities of disabilities in deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits. Identifying it as a learning disability or naming the specific learning disability is sufficient enough. Labeling a person as "slow" impacts their social status, confidence, and may not be accurate even with many learning disabilities. "Disability" is preferred because of its more inclusive nature normalizing individual experiences with various conditions and focusing on the need for accessibility as the root of disability. Slow does not account for accessibility. If somone receives accessibility support and taught in a different manner, they may learn skills as quick as their peers.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4254,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:33.610630','Portraying qualities of disabilities in deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits. Identifying it as a learning disability or naming the specific learning disability is sufficient enough. Labeling a person as "slow" impacts their social status, confidence, and may not be accurate even with many learning disabilities. Slow does not account for accessibility. If somone receives accessibility support and taught in a different manner, they may learn skills as quick as their peers.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4255,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:34.786755','Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits. Portraying a skill in a negative way assumes that the person cannot or won''t improve, however, many Disabled people can improve on skillsets with the appropriate accessibility support.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4256,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:35.950978','Portraying qualities, attitudes, behaviors, emotional states/responses of those with disabilities using deficit language disparages people for their natural brain processing traits. Portraying a skill in a negative way assumes that the person cannot or won''t improve, however, many Disabled people can improve on skillsets with the appropriate accessibility support.\ToClarify:
INSERT INTO "rules_rule" VALUES(4257,'2023-11-15','2023-11-15 16:05:38.529558','Dyslexia is a learning disability. The U.K is the only location that officially categorizes Dyslexia as a "learning difficulty" and this is largely argued within the disability community. The Dyslexic community is split and use both person-first and identity-first language.\ToClarify:
